  "body": "## What changed\n- Added `CornerRelief` (`None`, `Dogbone`, `TBone`), `TBoneDirection` (`LongEdge`, `ShortEdge`, `Horizontal`, `Vertical`), and per-corner `overrides` to `OpParams::Pocket`, `OpParams::Adaptive2D`, and `OpParams::Offset2D`.\n- Implemented inside-corner detection (with micro-fillet chord collapse) and relief spur splicing in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/corner_relief.rs` and `corner_relief_spur.rs`, plus corner-blend ban seeding in `pocket_emit.rs`.\n- Added operation safety checks in `crates/app/src/operation/corner_relief.rs` for stock bounds, `Exclude` and open far-side regions, `DoNotTouch` keepouts, kept/neighbour steel, and multi-height thin-wall punch-throughs.\n- Refused `Adaptive2D::Trochoidal` with active corner relief by name in `crates/app/src/operation/types/sane.rs`, `generate.rs`, and the UI panel.\n- Added strictly bounded verification corridors (`CornerReliefZone`) in `crates/sim/src/verify/corner_relief.rs`, `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/corner_relief.rs`, and `crates/app/src/operation/corner_relief_sim.rs`.\n- Wired project serialization, MCP `set_operation` round-trip, WCS yaw transforms, UI controls (`kind_editors.rs`, `mill2d_page.rs`), and the decision note in `docs/decisions/2400-corner-relief.md`.\n\n## Cause\nInside sharp corners of closed 2D pockets and square slots always leave unmachined corner fillets equal to the cutter radius. Adding opt-in bisector (`Dogbone`) or tangent (`TBone`) spurs extends the cutter center to the true corner reach while pre-emission guards and bounded verification zones block wall gouges and punch-throughs.\n\n## Review fixes\n\nReview head: `69ff095a59b5c3817de4ba01019bd98d41e010ba`.\nNew head: `fa0515aab4754d42992caedeff9b4e87f4cefb6d`.\n\n1. Relief exemptions now check the upper Z limit of swept contacts and contact points.\n   Full-verifier pins cover cutting edges and shanks above the relief, a ramp through its top, and an enclosed shank.\n   The suite also retains valid contact inside the relief and rapid collisions with stock.\n   Pins: `cutting_edge_above_relief_top_keeps_gouge` and `shank_above_relief_top_keeps_part_collision`.\n   The full `camcraft-sim --test corner_relief` suite passed all 6 tests.\n2. Model-link test fixtures now advance the modification time for each write.\n   The existing regression checks that its final edit keeps the file size and changes the modification time.\n   Pin: `model_link_tests::a_changed_file_is_imported_again_as_one_undo_step_and_its_operations_only_go_stale`.\n   Full UI library: GREEN, 1,277 passed, 0 failed, 7 ignored.\n   The suite ran from `crates/ui` with 6 threads.\n3. Structural tests cover the relief modes and all T-bone direction choices for Pocket, Adaptive2D, and Offset2D.\n   They also check draft isolation, Apply, and undo.\n   Pins: `relief_modes_and_direction_controls_edit_each_supported_passes_page` and `relief_mode_and_direction_apply_as_one_undoable_command`.\n   UI images show the actual egui Pocket Passes fixture.\n   The before capture omits only the new corner relief editor call to reproduce the pre-feature panel.\n   The after captures render the production Dogbone and T-bone controls.\n   These images show the panel controls only.\n\n   ![Before: Pocket Passes without corner relief controls](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/231d050ac5f35fe2d5a59bcd6457e5460582a790/pr-2833/corner-relief-before.png)\n\n   ![After: Dogbone controls](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/231d050ac5f35fe2d5a59bcd6457e5460582a790/pr-2833/corner-relief-after-dogbone.png)\n\n   ![After: T-bone controls](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/231d050ac5f35fe2d5a59bcd6457e5460582a790/pr-2833/corner-relief-after-tbone.png)\n\n4. Reached heavy lanes: GREEN, 220 steps, 0 unexpected failures.\n   The plan ran one release build, 33 motion steps, and 186 app steps.\n   Three #1950 checks were RED as expected.\n   Command: `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`.\n5. Shared fixtures, serialization, and cutting/safety tests now use separate files below 400 lines.\n   All seven original test bodies remain.\n   Pin: `corner_relief_test_modules_stay_under_the_line_law`.\n   Split app suites: 8 passed (cutting 4, safety 3, serialization 1).\n\n### Review-fix mutation checks\n\n- Verifier upper Z checks: All four collision regressions were RED after source reversion. Both controls stayed GREEN. All six tests passed after restoration.\n- Model-link timestamp isolation: RED with the original equal-size, equal-timestamp rewrite. GREEN after restoration.\n- Relief direction controls: RED when the production relief editor call was omitted. GREEN after restoration. Both structural tests and the model-link regression passed.\n- Split test file sizes: RED with 652 lines in the safety test file. GREEN after restoration.\n\n### Existing known failures\n\nThe gate ran these three checks separately. Each was RED as expected under issue #1950:\n\n- `machining2d::pocket_hsm::ring_tests::the_stock_ring_level_reaches_the_air_planner_with_the_stock`\n- `machining2d::pocket_hsm::ring_tests::the_stock_ring_level_plans_adaptive_with_no_budget_note`\n- `the_users_whole_model_bore_roughs_adaptive_on_each_level` (`camcraft-app --test pocket3d_hsm`)\n\nThe remaining 216 heavy test steps passed. The release build also passed.\n\n### Final checks\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: GREEN, 779 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: GREEN, all four touched crates and all targets, with `-D warnings`.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: GREEN, 220 steps, 0 unexpected failures.\n   The plan ran one release build, 33 motion steps, and 186 app steps.\n   Three #1950 checks were RED as expected.\n\n## Goldens moved\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/pocket_waterline_square_dogbone.cl` (new golden, 28 lines, 26 moves showing dogbone relief corners at `±7879` um for a 6 mm flat end mill in a 20 mm square pocket).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full release gate (`SLOW_BINARIES`), the pixel snapshot lane, and interactive GUI corner selection.\n\n## Overlaps\n- Touches `crates/app/src/mcp/edit.rs` in a different function (`corner_relief_kept` vs `add_tool`/`set_stock` in `#2773`); whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: Add dogbone and T-bone inside-corner relief for closed 2D pockets and square slots.\nFixes #2400\n\n",
